\subsubsection{Backflip}
For complex motion tasks such as backflip, a phase-based training approach is adopted following the method in \cite{kim2024stage}. The environment maintains a finite state machine (FSM) with five discrete phases: \textit{Stand}, \textit{Crouch}, \textit{Jump}, \textit{Air}, and \textit{Land}, as illustrated in Fig.~\ref{fig:FSM}. Transitions between phases are primarily determined by the robot's height and foot contact states.

