\[ M(v_s) = (cpu\_usage, memory\_usage, request\_rate, latency) \]

Each resource node $v_r \in \text{Resources}$ has metadata:
\[ M(v_r) = (capacity, utilization, performance\_score, cost) \]

Hyperedges $E$ represent service deployments, where each edge contains:
\[ e_i = \{\text{service}_1, ..., \text{service}_k, \text{resource}_1, ..., \text{resource}_m\} \]

Edge metadata includes:
\[ M(e) = (total\_load, reliability\_score, cost\_efficiency) \]

\subsection{Operator Definitions}

Define key operators $\Omega = \{\omega_{load}, \omega_{perf}, \omega_{cost}\}$:

1. Load Balancing Operator:
\[ f_{load}(v,e) = \begin{cases}
    \frac{M(v).cpu\_usage}{M(e).total\_load} & \text{if } v \in \text{Services} \\
    1 - \frac{M(v).utilization}{M(v).capacity} & \text{if } v \in \text{Resources}
\end{cases} \]

2. Performance Operator:
\[ f_{perf}(v,e) = \begin{cases}
    \frac{1}{M(v).latency} \cdot M(e).reliability\_score & \text{if } v \in \text{Services} \\
    M(v).performance\_score & \text{if } v \in \text{Resources}
\end{cases} \]

3. Cost Efficiency Operator:
\[ f_{cost}(v,e) = \begin{cases}
    \frac{M(v).request\_rate}{M(v).memory\_usage} & \text{if } v \in \text{Services} \\
    \frac{M(v).capacity}{M(v).cost} & \text{if } v \in \text{Resources}
\end{cases} \]

\subsection{Combined Ranking Function}

The relevance function combines these operators:
\[ R(v,e) = w_{load}f_{load}(v,e) + w_{perf}f_{perf}(v,e) + w_{cost}f_{cost}(v,e) \]

where weights are determined by system priorities:
\[ w_{load} = 0.4, w_{perf} = 0.35, w_{cost} = 0.25 \]

