\section{Experimental results}
\label{sec:results}

In this section, we present the results of the experiments, split by dataset. In each dataset, we first analyze the influence of the number of training epochs during offspring generation, $n_t$, and then the population and the size of the offspring, $\mu$ and $\lambda$, respectively (\textbf{RQ1}). We also show the results obtained by a standard SSL-GAN (\textbf{RQ2}). Thirty independent runs were performed in all the cases, except in the analysis of the sensitivity of the methods to the number of labels (\textbf{RQ3}) in \MNIST, where 15 independent runs were performed.


