Although we treat the training problem as a single-objective problem, discriminator training could be formulated using a multi-objective approach, where supervised and unsupervised losses, are considered as two different objectives of the training process. Besides, \method\  could be implemented using parallelism.
In addition, it would be interesting to analyze the influence of the spatial distribution of the population in the performance of the GAN. This could be done comparing the results of \method\ with that of Lipizzaner~\cite{DBLP:journals/asc/ToutouhNHO23}.

