Assume that $\beta \leq \frac{1}{2N \mathcal{R} d}$ for some  $N>0$, then each operator $$M_i = e^{\beta H^{S_i}/2}e^{-\beta H^{S_{i-1}}/2}$$ and correspondingly $M_i^\dag$ is a probability distribution over operators of the form $I+(N\mathcal{R})^{-t_k}\Gamma_k$, where for any $k$, $\Gamma_k \in \mathcal{M}^*  \cup \{0\}$ is $t_k\mathcal{R}$-local and is supported on $S_{i-1}$. 
