% 4. Dynamic flight varying between 3m and 15m, alternating between \gls{los} and \gls{nlos}.

During each phase, the \gls{uav} transmits both flight and \gls{uav} telemetry data, as well as video streams at different resolutions: 480p, 720p, and 1080p. To comply with regulations, the drone is manually controlled by a pilot who handles takeoff, the \gls{uav} maintains an altitude of 1.5m via lidar-based altitude control until it lands. In the dynamic scenario, the pilot also controls the \gls{uav}'s movements.


