\section{Proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:basins of attraction_vnvp_consensus}}\label{app:thm:basins of attraction_vnvp_consensus}
%The proof establishes that, if the partitions $\mathcal{V}_{1}^{+}(0)$ and $\mathcal{V}_{-1}^{-}(0)$ satisfy \eqref{eq:condition_consensus_VnVp_coo_thm}, then the following three statements hold true for all  $t\geq 0$: i) $\delta_i(\vect{z}(t))\geq0$, for all $i\in\mathcal V_1^+(0)$, and $\delta_i(\vect{z}(t))>0$, for all $i\in\mathcal V_{-1}^+(0)$; ii) $\vect x(t+1)\geq \vect x(t)$; and iii) $\vect{y}(t+1)\geq 0$.
For the sake of convenience in our proof, we define positive constants $p=2\lambda\beta(1-\lambda)$ and $q=2\lambda(1-\beta)$.
The proof is based on the following set of arguments. If the partitions $\mathcal{V}_{1}^{+}(0)$ and $\mathcal{V}_{-1}^{-}(0)$ satisfy
