\subsection{Experiment Details}
For the training of \impulsep{ImPulSe+}, all original CT images were downsampled to a resolution of $128^{3}$, and the HU value of input CT scans is clipped between $-1000$ and $400$. This pre-processing is also applied to the modeling of FCN, DeepLabv3, and nnUNet with low-resolution input, as well as the pretraining of the template network. During the training stage, the number of points sampled for each case is $16^{3}$. The AdamW optimizer is adopted to train both models except nnUNet, and a combination of cross-entropy and Dice loss as the loss function. The initial learning rate is set at $0.001$ and CosineAnnealingLR is used to adjust the learning rate, with a lower bound of $10^{-6}$. The setting of the optimizer, loss function, and scheduler of the pretraining of the template network is aligned with \impulsep{ImPulSe+}, and the batch size of the pretraining process is 8.

The training and inference of nnUNet utilize a 3D full-resolution U-Net architecture in two different resolution inputs (original-resolution and $128^{3}$), both using a 5-fold training approach. The results presented do not include post-processing for nnUNet. The optimizer is SGD and the initial learning rate was set at $0.01$ and decayed by a factor of $3e^{−5}$.

The experiments are based on the implementation of PyTorch 1.11.1 and Python 3.9, on a machine with 4 NVIDIA 3090 GPUs, Intel(R) Xeon(R) CPU @ 2.20 GHz, and 128 GB memory. 
