 Let $(\loc, \clockval) = \Init(\runs'(\vrun))$.

 \LongVersion{For $\fml = \LAST(\action^1_{\vrun}) - \LAST(\action^2_{\vrun}) \compOp \lterm$,}
 \LongVersion{by}\ShortVersion{By} the construction of $\observerof{\fml}$,
 we have $\clockval(\action^1) = \recordval(\action^1)$ and $\clockval(\action^2) = \recordval(\action^2)$.
 Moreover, by the definition of $\Label$,
 we have $\clockval(\action^1) - \clockval(\action^2) \compOp \lterm \iff \fml \in \Label(\loc)$.
 Thus, by the semantics of \ExtPTCTL{},
